    <GaugingStation location="Huntly" name="Deveron" number="9010">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">Velocity area station gauging a natural, rural catchment.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">One peak flow rating across period of record, gauged to just over 3m, with a measured flow of 135 cumecs. Flows are based on simple extrapolation beyond the highest gauging.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">20m open channel with full cableway. Gravel boulder and rock control. Station added to peak flows dataset in September 2019 (WINFAP Files v8).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Natural catchment with no significant storage.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">Significant arable and pasture agriculture in lower reaches with rough grazing, moorland and peat bog in the upper catchment.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff"/>
        </Comments>
        <Usages>
            <Usage notes="Well gauged to QMED." suitable="Yes" type="QMED"/>
            <Usage notes="Calibration based on gauging up to 3.039m, then simple extrapolation thereafter. The flood gaugings provide some confidence in the Peak Flow data." suitable="Yes" type="Pooling"/>
        </Usages>
    </GaugingStation>
